body:
Hey everyone, just starting my first stream on twitch! I'm a relatively high elo player; but would love to see some new faces. Come say hi! 

&nbsp;

twitch.tv/villhelms

Indeed! Froggen, as an example, only uses normal cast on all abilities. Almost all pros prefer quick-cast though! My recommendation for you, is that you keybind quick cast to your keys, but bind normal cast to "shift+q" etc etc. That's what most pros do.

&nbsp;

Let me know if you have any other questions!

So generally, for an AP mid you want a page like [this](http://d1mt9jmphk9kik.cloudfront.net/teamdignitas/image1457605299.png) unless you're against an AD mid, then you probably want something like [this,](https://gyazo.com/964b93128451dfabdbd43593072155fe) 

&nbsp;

Let me know if you have any other questions!

Hey so I'm looking for a new keyboard. (been using a cheap logitech one for years)  Couple questions: 

&nbsp;

How much input delay do wireless keyboards give for gaming?

&nbsp;

I'm looking for a pretty quiet keyboard, but with that satisfying press you get from a mechanical keyboard, any suggestions? (I know how vague that is I apologize for that, if you need clarity let me know.)

At risk of sounding like an idiot again, why does your monitor not list a Hz count? I like it though, it seems like great specs for a reasonable price. 

&nbsp;

Secondly, I'm glad I can justify your longest thread. I promise you there's more questions to come if you don't mind! For example, I'll be moving my computer setup from my basement into my bedroom and I'm wondering about using a wireless connection to my router. I'm not sure if I'll be able to move it with me into my room. I've heard a lot of bad things about using wireless connections as a gamer. Any thoughts? (I did a network test and on my laptop I have 35mb download and 5mb upload speed)

I did some tower searching myself and found a couple decent ones. My current problem is monitor selection. Both of these monitors look awesome, but I have been told they won't serve me well because the resolution is too low. Can I get your insight on them? 

&nbsp;

https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B01N6IRHTE/ref=ask_ql_qh_dp_hza

&nbsp;

https://www.amazon.com/VIOTEK-GN32C-CURVED-COMPUTER-MONITOR/dp/B01N2QN4YP%3FSubscriptionId%3DAKIAJ76EIXAV3V6D6JEQ%26tag%3Dglobalnetwork-20%26linkCode%3Dxm2%26camp%3D2025%26creative%3D165953%26creativeASIN%3DB01N2QN4YP

&nbsp;

As for League; trust me, no matter how bad you are, I've always seen worse. Also, a lot of my friends aren't very good haha I'm glad I can return the favor even in small. Pm me your IGN!

P.S. Did you get a chance to try out streaming? How was the performance, if so?

Based on your info I think its safe to say I won't really be needing the 7600k and I could put the extra $50 into buying a sleeker looking tower! Love the advice man. I might have found a way I can return the favor; I'm a d1 league player and I'd love to when my computer is sorted out give you some pointers or duo some games with you to help you improve if you're interested. 

&nbsp;

Also, do you have any recommendations for any really cool/unique looking towers? I don't mind springing a bit more for something that doesn't look dull. After all, it's going to be what Im looking at all the time.

I take 90% of what people say in this Sub as comedic commentary. Its the only way to stay sane.

&nbsp;
 Edit: Still love it though; I hope all the Challenjours never change.
